                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Tengami was boring, empty, and not worth the price.\n\nI loved the pop-up storybook concept, and some of the scenery was pretty, but being sorta pretty wasn't enough to make me enjoy playing it. The world felt empty, the graphics had this gritty look I didn't care for, and the whole thing never pulled me in.\n\nThe puzzles somehow managed to feel too easy and confusing at the same time, which mostly left me annoyed instead of satisfied.\n\nCool idea, weak execution.",
